<<~ ahu slot=`#/wave-2-hand-back`>>

! Wave 2 hand-back

''Seed progress.'' `seed.ts` now prints a per-holding start and completion line, recursive carrier counts, elapsed time, 5-second INGEST settle ticks, a folded CREATE line by default, and a final `seed: N/N holdings · XmYYs` tally. Retry guidance marks successful and diff-gated INGEST runs safe; failed act runs direct the operator to the request/change-id hint. Durations use `performance.now()`, matching the CLI's existing process-local monotonic liveness seam (`stand.ts` and `port-control.ts`); no new wall-clock dependency was introduced.

''Shim errors.'' Both host shims keep census output quiet by default and show it only with `LARES_DEBUG=1`. A census refusal says the vessel remains standing and directs the operator to logs and another `down`. Failed `up` preserves Compose's error and appends the requested readiness/retry sentence.

''Vault unlock.'' Unknown custody answers now say unlock did not complete and point to `lares vault status`; human and JSON error output omit the raw answer and internal reading label. `--verbose` is registered as a vessel flag and documented for seed CREATE detail.

''Checks.'' Build and stamp passed (<code>&#64;lares/cli</code>, final stamp `412360ae0285a744…`); CLI typecheck passed. Final focused CLI run: 4 files, 134 tests passed. Full CLI run: 163/164 files and 1823/1824 tests passed; `port-control.test.ts` had one 5-second timeout under full worker load, then passed alone (1 file, 22 tests). Shim suite: 103/103 passed across `.sh` and `.ps1`. Evergreen boundary passed (3874 files). `rite-commands-witness.sh` passed (13 commands, 13 sub-doors, 7 symbols). `git diff --check` passed.

''WAIT for a later wave.'' Found end-hang measure: time CLI exit separately from Compose run teardown. Founding-copy glosses: route, seed charter, chair, place, persona zero, generation, holding, carrier, and `alreadyStood`.

